WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.727
This query joins patients with admissions.

00:00:02.727 --> 00:00:08.742
The name is trimmed, repeated whitespace is collapsed, and display case is applied.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:12.762
The email domain is extracted from a normalized email.

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:15.607
Admission time is reduced to month grain.

00:00:15.607 --> 00:00:18.947
Length of stay is converted to numeric days.

00:00:18.947 --> 00:00:23.867
Read the query column by column rather than as one large block.

00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:29.392
Connect this idea to an operations team aligning timestamps across locations.

00:00:29.392 --> 00:00:35.382
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.382 --> 00:00:43.217
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:48.837
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:48.837 --> 00:00:54.678
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
